#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:6
msgid "# Sleep Mechanism"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:8
msgid ""
"> Light Sleep is the incremental extraction channel (semantic + limbic + "
"autobiographical); Deep Sleep optimizes semantic memory inventory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:10
msgid "## Overview"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:12
msgid ""
"Sleep is the digital life's memory consolidation mechanism—analogous to "
"human sleep where the brain replays daytime experiences, converts short-term "
"memory to long-term storage; the consolidation process itself dissipates, "
"leaving no trace."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:19
msgid ""
"**Internal mechanism, no trace** — Sleep runs in background, does not write "
"to sessions, does not affect conversation flow"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:19
msgid ""
"**Do not copy human rhythm literally** — Triggered by system need (cron), "
"not real-time"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:19
msgid ""
"**Two-tier layering** — Light sleep (incremental writes: semantic / limbic / "
"autobiographical), deep sleep (semantic inventory optimization) each with "
"its role"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:19
msgid ""
"**Identity context** — All memory processing must carry **self layer six "
"blocks** + resident memory (see [`self-layer.md`](self-layer.md))"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:21
msgid "## Current State"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:26
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Mechanism        | Status         | Notes                              |\n"
"| ---------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n"
"| Light sleep cron | ✅ Implemented | Daily 02:00, `builtin-light-sleep` |\n"
"| Deep sleep cron  | ✅ Implemented | Daily 03:00, `builtin-deep-sleep`  |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:28
msgid "## Light Sleep"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:35
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Attribute     | Value                                                                                                                          |\n"
"| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| Trigger       | Cron only, daily 02:00 (`0 2 * * *`), no manual trigger                                                                        |\n"
"| Scope         | Sessions with activity in previous CST calendar day (`sessions.updated_at`)                                                    |\n"
"| Input         | Full day's conversations (user+assistant, tools stripped), segmented by session                                                |\n"
"| Orchestration | Three stages sequential (peer stages, separate LLM calls each; zero tool calls in prior stage does not skip subsequent stages) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:37
msgid "### Three Stages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Stage              | Target storage                      | Tool allowlist                                    | Input highlights                                                         |\n"
"| ------------------ | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| 1 Semantic         | `semantic_memory`                   | `memory_semantic_create` / `update` / `deprecate` | Conversation + existing semantic (`listBySourceSessions`)                |\n"
"| 2 Limbic           | `limbic_memory`                     | `memory_limbic_create`                            | Conversation + existing limbic (`listBySession`)                         |\n"
"| 3 Autobiographical | `autobiographical_memory`           | `memory_autobiographical_create` / `deprecate`    | Conversation + day's semantic + day's limbic + existing autobiographical |\n"
"| 3b                 | `self_blocks.autobiography_summary` | (programmatic compression, no LLM)                | Active autobiographical narratives → summary block refresh               |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Restraint principle:** Each stage LLM judges \"nothing worth recording\" → no tool calls, reply skip; program does not skip subsequent stages because prior stage had zero tool calls.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Dedup (semantic):** **Local only**—compare only against existing memories with same `source_sessions`; cross-thread merging left to deep sleep.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:50
msgid ""
"Implementation: [`capabilities/memory/src/light-sleep/run.ts`](../../"
"capabilities/memory/src/light-sleep/run.ts); wiring: [`serve.ts`](../../"
"service/service/src/serve.ts)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:52
msgid "### Stage 1 Message Structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:54
msgid ""
"System prompt: self layer six blocks + resident memory (pinned facts, top "
"20)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:60
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| #   | Content                                                                                              |\n"
"| --- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| 1   | Full day's conversation: user+assistant, segmented by session ID, with timestamps and context labels |\n"
"| 2   | Existing memories: `listBySourceSessions` pre-filter (active memories intersecting day's sessions)   |\n"
"| 3   | Semantic extraction instructions + three-tool usage                                                  |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:62
msgid ""
"LLM **does not** carry `memory_semantic_search` (message 2 already provided "
"by program)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:64
msgid "### `memory_semantic_update` Semantics (Overwrite)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:68
msgid "**Only modifies passed fields**; omitted fields unchanged"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:68
msgid "To clear `source_sessions` → explicitly pass `source_sessions: []`"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:68
msgid "Omit `source_sessions` → keep original value"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:70
msgid "### Flow"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:80
msgid ""
"``` 1. Compute CST previous-day time window 2. listSessionIdsUpdatedBetween "
"→ involved session list 3. Stage 1: semantic extraction → semantic_memory 4. "
"Stage 2: limbic extraction → limbic_memory 5. Stage 3: autobiographical "
"narrative extraction → autobiographical_memory 6. Stage 3b: compression "
"refresh → self_blocks.autobiography_summary 7. Write light_sleep_state.json "
"```"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:82
msgid "### Context Too Large"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:84
msgid ""
"When single input exceeds ~120k characters, truncate by session `updated_at` "
"descending, append `[Truncated N sessions]` at conversation segment end "
"(same truncation logic reused across stages)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:86
msgid "## Deep Sleep"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:93
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Attribute  | Value                                                                                                       |\n"
"| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Trigger    | Cron only, daily 03:00 (`0 3 * * *`), no manual trigger                                                     |\n"
"| Target     | All active `semantic_memory`                                                                                |\n"
"| Operations | Contradiction detection + expiry marking, split, dedup merge—three sequential rounds                        |\n"
"| Tools      | `memory_semantic_create` / `memory_semantic_update` / `memory_semantic_deprecate` / `memory_semantic_merge` |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:95
msgid "### Three Rounds"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:101
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Round | Intent                                   | Focus                                                                  |\n"
"| ----- | ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| 1     | Contradiction detection + expiry marking | Exclusive contradictions → deprecate; superseded facts → deprecate     |\n"
"| 2     | Split                                    | One content with multiple independent facts → split into multiple rows |\n"
"| 3     | Dedup merge                              | Duplicate/highly similar → merge into one                              |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:103
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Ordering rationale:** Clean problems first (contradiction+expiry), then refine (split), then merge. Each round sees clean data after prior rounds.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:105
msgid "### Contradiction Definition (Exclusive)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:107
msgid ""
"Two memories semantically negate each other and cannot be explained by "
"temporal change → contradiction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:112
msgid ""
"✓ Contradiction: \"daughter born Year of Tiger\" vs \"daughter born Year of "
"Goat\" (zodiac unique)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:112
msgid ""
"✓ Contradiction: \"dislikes spicy food\" vs \"likes spicy food\" (direct "
"negation)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:112
msgid ""
"✗ Not contradiction: \"likes apples\" vs \"likes cherries\" (can coexist)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:112
msgid ""
"✗ Not contradiction (change): \"likes Python\" vs \"now prefers TypeScript\" "
"(both can be valid)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:114
msgid "### Message Structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:116
msgid "System prompt: self layer six blocks + resident memory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| #   | Content                          | Notes                                                                                           |\n"
"| --- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| 1   | Full active semantic memory JSON | **Identical every round → provider cache**                                                      |\n"
"| 1.5 | Incremental change summary       | Empty first round; subsequent rounds append prior operations (merged/deprecated/added/modified) |\n"
"| 2   | Program pre-filter               | Empty in v1                                                                                     |\n"
"| 3   | Instructions                     | Round intent + tool usage                                                                       |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:125
msgid ""
"Message 1 is the token hog and grows linearly; kept unchanged to maximize "
"provider cache."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:127
msgid "### Message 1.5 Format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:130
msgid "``` # Incremental changes (this content is authoritative)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:134
msgid ""
"## Processed (ignore these original entries in message 1)  f-001 — merged "
"into f-003 f-010 — expired/deprecated (superseded by new fact)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:137
msgid ""
"## New entries (not in message 1)  f-003 (world) \"Bob works in Pudong, "
"Shanghai\" sources=[s-abc,s-def] observed=2026-05-01T..."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:141
msgid ""
"## Modified entries (authoritative here, overrides message 1)  f-030 — "
"modified: content updated to \"...\" ```"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:143
msgid "### Threshold Strategy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:150
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Full JSON size | Behavior                       |\n"
"| -------------- | ------------------------------ |\n"
"| < 10k          | Normal                         |\n"
"| 10k ~ 100k     | ⚠️ warn log, normal processing |\n"
"| 100k ~ 300k    | Batch by type                  |\n"
"| > 300k         | ❌ error, refuse               |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:152
msgid "### `merge_semantic_memories` Tool"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:154
msgid "Program auto-stitches fields; LLM only cares about merged new content:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:159
msgid "`source_sessions` → union deduped across source memories"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:159
msgid "`observed_at` → earliest value"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:159
msgid "Create new memory → deprecate all source_ids"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:159
msgid "Only 1 source_id → prompt to use update_semantic_memory"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:161
msgid "### Operation Log"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:163
msgid ""
"Each round written to `~/.anima/logs/deep_sleep_{day}_{round_index}"
"_{round}.json`, not in database, for troubleshooting only."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:165
msgid ""
"Records: date, round, active memory count, prior change count, tool_calls "
"count, summary, change log snapshot."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:167
msgid "## Trigger Mechanism"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:173
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```cron\n"
"0 2 * * *  light-sleep           # builtin-light-sleep (semantic + limbic + autobiographical)\n"
"0 3 * * *  deep-sleep            # builtin-deep-sleep\n"
"30 5 * * *  memory-reference-sync  # builtin-memory-reference-sync\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:175
msgid "After downtime, next scheduled run catches up; not a real-time system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:177
msgid "## Historical Backfill (One-Time CLI)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:179
msgid ""
"For historical conversations before go-live or after migration, run light "
"sleep **per CST calendar day**, same logic as nightly cron but manually "
"triggered with separate progress file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:183
msgid ""
"```bash anima memory sleep backfill [--from YYYY-MM-DD] [--to YYYY-MM-DD] [--"
"resume] ```"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:189
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Option     | Description                                                              |\n"
"| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n"
"| `--from`   | Start date; if omitted, earliest non-debug session CST day in `sessions` |\n"
"| `--to`     | End date; if omitted, **yesterday CST** (same as 02:00 cron default day) |\n"
"| `--resume` | Continue from progress file, skip completed days                         |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:191
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Progress file:** `~/.anima/runtime/light_sleep_backfill_state.json` (separate from `light_sleep_state.json`).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:193
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Behavior notes:**\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:200
msgid ""
"Each day independently calls `runLightSleep({ day })`; single-day failure "
"recorded then continue next day"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:200
msgid ""
"Stage 3b (autobiography summary refresh) runs only on **last day** by "
"default; skipped on intermediate days to save tokens"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:200
msgid ""
"Before backfill, ensure LLM correctly fills `observed_at` / `occurred_at` "
"(see [`memory.md`](memory.md)); otherwise memory times become backfill moment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:200
msgid ""
"Backfill only writes semantic / limbic / autobiographical; **cross-session "
"semantic merge still relies on deep sleep**—after backfill, wait for 03:00 "
"deep sleep or trigger manually"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:200
msgid ""
"No conflict with 02:00 cron, but pause service or avoid early-morning window "
"during backfill"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:200
msgid ""
"Single conversation input still capped at ~**120k characters** (see "
"\"Context Too Large\" above)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:202
msgid ""
"Implementation: [`capabilities/memory/src/light-sleep/backfill.ts`](../../"
"capabilities/memory/src/light-sleep/backfill.ts); CLI bootstrap: [`bootstrap-"
"memory-jobs.ts`](../../service/service/src/bootstrap-memory-jobs.ts)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:204
msgid "## Relationship to Existing Architecture"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:219
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"PG messages (conversation archive)\n"
"  │ light sleep cron (02:00, three stages)\n"
"  ├─► semantic_memory\n"
"  ├─► limbic_memory\n"
"  └─► autobiographical_memory ──compress──► self_blocks.autobiography_summary\n"
"  │\n"
"  │ deep sleep cron (03:00, semantic maintenance)\n"
"  ▼\n"
"semantic_memory (consolidated)\n"
"  │ memory_recall (real-time retrieval in conversation)\n"
"  ▼\n"
"Agent identity and recalled fragments in current context\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:221
msgid ""
"`session:updated` EventBus event retained (WebUI refresh, etc.), **no "
"longer** triggers reflect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:223
msgid "## `memory_remember` Tool"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/concepts/sleep.md:224
msgid ""
"In-conversation `memory_remember` is a convenience wrapper: auto-infers "
"`source_sessions` (current session) and `observed_at`, underlying "
"`memory_semantic_create` logic. Physical delete via `action=delete`; soft "
"deprecation via `memory_semantic_deprecate`."
msgstr ""
